    {
      "id": "claim_e287c36ca393422fbaa4fbe466dc026f",
      "statement": "Connection resolution reads a usable token from the connected Cloudflare gatekeeper account via getUsableAccessToken, auto-selects the billing account when the grant sees exactly one, and serves a fresh cached credit balance without hitting the API within the cache TTL; a null/unreadable balance is treated as not-funded so the system falls back to the free tier rather than attempting a BYOK call that would fail.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://packages/workshop-backend/src/ai-gateway-billing/cloudflare/connection-service.ts#L60-L130",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:07bf41111dfb16587c0e24c2f82c92aa6637a418895d71314245dbadb9cdd911:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_df747162aafd456c9a3919119af86f85",
      "statement": "The decision tree: connected + balance >= the $2 default minimum bills the user's own gateway and does NOT consume the daily counter (reserving the platform free tier for others); otherwise the platform free tier consumes one daily call (consumeDailyLlmCall is atomic per UTC day and no-ops once exhausted so a blocked request never counts), and an exhausted counter blocks with a connect prompt (not connected) or a top-up prompt (connected but under-funded).",
